---
import LandingLayout from '../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';

// TIM: confirm or remove price line
const REVVIA_STARTING_PRICE_LINE =
  'Revvia engagements typically start around $3,500/month, and you pay ad platforms directly.';

const decision = [
  ['Under $1M', 'DIY + targeted help'],
  ['$1M – $5M', 'Fractional CMO'],
  ['$5M – $20M', 'Fractional CMO, or fractional plus an in-house coordinator'],
  ['$20M+', 'In-house leader plus specialist partners'],
];
---
<LandingLayout
  title="Hire, Agency, or Fractional? The Real Cost of Marketing Help in San Diego"
  description="A hire, an agency, or a fractional CMO - what each really costs in San Diego, what you get, and which fits your stage."
  path="/guides/real-cost"
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="guide">
    <div class="guide-actions no-print">
      <button type="button" class="guide-pdf" id="print-guide">Download as PDF</button>
    </div>

    <header class="guide-head">
      <p class="guide-eyebrow">Revvia Guide</p>
      <h1>Hire, Agency, or Fractional?</h1>
      <p class="guide-dek">The real cost of marketing help in San Diego - what each option costs, what you actually get, and how to tell which one your business needs right now.</p>
    </header>

    <p>Most owners of growing businesses hit the same wall: the marketing needs to get more serious, and you have three ways to make that happen. Hire someone. Bring on an agency. Or use a fractional marketing leader. They cost very different amounts and they solve very different problems. Here's the honest version.</p>

    <!-- VERIFY: confirm both medians on data.bls.gov/oes before launch -->
    <h2>Option A: Hire full-time</h2>
    <p>The real number is not the salary - it's the fully loaded cost once you add payroll taxes, benefits, software, and overhead. Start with federal wage data for our metro:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Marketing Managers</strong> - median annual wage <strong>$174,840</strong> (BLS OEWS, May 2025, San Diego–Chula Vista–Carlsbad metro).</li>
      <li><strong>Market Research Analysts &amp; Marketing Specialists</strong> - median <strong>$79,440</strong> (same source).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Per the BLS Employer Costs for Employee Compensation (June 2026), benefits run about <strong>30% of total compensation</strong> for private-industry workers. Dividing the wage by 0.70 gives an estimated fully loaded cost:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>About <strong>$250,000/yr</strong> for a marketing manager (estimate).</li>
      <li>About <strong>$113,000/yr</strong> for a specialist (estimate).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Treat those as estimates, not quotes - your actual cost depends on benefits, bonus, and tools. And here's the honest caveat: one person rarely covers strategy, ads, content, design, video, and analytics. Hire a manager and you still need people to execute. Hire a specialist and you still need someone to own the plan.</p>

    <h2>Option B: Hire an agency</h2>
    <p>Agencies get work done, and the right one is worth it. But know the typical pattern before you sign. Most agencies are channel specialists - they run ads, or SEO, or social - and they're paid to execute what they're told. That leaves you, the owner, as the de facto strategist: the one connecting the channels, setting the budget, and deciding what matters this quarter. The work ships. But nobody above the channel level owns the overall plan, and that's usually the thing that was actually missing.</p>

    <h2>Option C: Fractional CMO</h2>
    <p>A fractional CMO is senior marketing leadership - plus the team that executes - on a part-time basis, at a fraction of the cost of a full-time leader. You get someone who owns the strategy, the budget, and the number, working alongside the people who do the work, without a six-figure hire and the overhead that comes with it.</p>
    <p>That's how Revvia works: founder-led, in person in San Diego, month to month, with strategy and execution in one place. One team owns the plan and runs the channels, and you have one person accountable for results.</p>
    <!-- TIM: confirm or remove price line -->
    <p class="guide-price">{REVVIA_STARTING_PRICE_LINE}</p>

    <h2>Which one fits your stage</h2>
    <p>A simple rule of thumb. This is our recommendation, not a statistic.</p>
    <table class="guide-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Annual revenue</th><th>Our recommendation</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {decision.map(([stage, rec]) => (
          <tr><td>{stage}</td><td>{rec}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>The next step</h2>
    <p>Not sure where you land? Two quick ways to find out.</p>
    <div class="guide-cta no-print">
      <a class="lp-btn" href="/scorecard">Take the 10-minute scorecard →</a>
      <a class="lp-link" href="/contact">Talk it through on a call →</a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="guide-sources-h">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="guide-sources">
      <li>BLS Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS), May 2025 - <a href="https://www.bls.gov/oes/" rel="nofollow">bls.gov/oes</a> (San Diego–Chula Vista–Carlsbad metro).</li>
      <li>BLS Employer Costs for Employee Compensation (ECEC), June 2026 - <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ecec/" rel="nofollow">bls.gov/ecec</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</LandingLayout>

<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('print-guide')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
</script>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 80px; }
  .guide-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .guide-pdf {
    background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); color: #fff; border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 10px 16px; font: 600 14px Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .guide-pdf:hover { border-color: var(--m); }
  .guide-head { margin: 10px 0 30px; }
  .guide-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; color: var(--muted-2); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .guide h1 { font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px); line-height: 1.05; }
  .guide-dek { color: var(--muted); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 14px; }
  .guide h2 { font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 28px); letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 40px 0 12px; color: #fff; }
  .guide p { color: #d7dae2; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .guide p strong, .guide li strong { color: #fff; }
  .guide ul { margin: 0 0 18px; padding-left: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .guide li { color: #d7dae2; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 24px; position: relative; }
  .guide li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 10px; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--grad); }
  .guide-price { border-left: 3px solid var(--m); padding-left: 16px; color: #fff; font-weight: 500; }
  .guide-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0 18px; }
  .guide-table th, .guide-table td { text-align: left; padding: 13px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 16px; }
  .guide-table th { color: var(--muted-2); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .guide-table td:first-child { font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; white-space: nowrap; }
  .guide-table td { color: #d7dae2; }
  .guide-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 20px; margin: 10px 0 20px; }
  .lp-btn { background: var(--grad); color: #fff; border: 0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 24px; font: 600 15.5px Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; }
  .lp-link { color: var(--m); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .guide-sources-h { font-size: 18px !important; }
  .guide-sources li { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
  .guide-sources a { color: var(--m); }
</style>

<style is:global>
  @media print {
    .lp-head, .lp-foot, .skip-link, .guide-actions, .guide-cta { display: none !important; }
    html, body { background: #fff !important; }
    .guide, .guide h1, .guide h2, .guide p, .guide li, .guide td, .guide th, .guide-dek, .guide-eyebrow {
      color: #000 !important;
    }
    .guide li::before { background: #000 !important; }
    .guide-price { border-left-color: #000 !important; }
    .guide-table th, .guide-table td { border-color: #666 !important; }
    .guide-sources a, .guide a { color: #000 !important; text-decoration: underline; }
  }
</style>
